NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002612 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002613 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002614 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002615 "=head2 Where can I go for help?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002616 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002617 "For questions about installation or usage, please ask on the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002618 "dbi-users@perl.org mailing list (see http://dbi.perl.org) or post a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002619 "question on PerlMonks (L<http://www.perlmonks.org/>, where Jeff is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002620 "known as jZed).  Jens does not visit PerlMonks on a regular basis."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002621 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002622 "If you have a bug report, a patch or a suggestion, please open a new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002623 "report ticket at CPAN (but please check previous reports first in case"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002624 "your issue has already been addressed). You can mail any of the module"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002625 "maintainers, but you are more assured of an answer by posting to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002626 "the dbi-users list or reporting the issue in RT."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002627 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002628 "Report tickets should contain a detailed description of the bug or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002629 "enhancement request and at least an easily verifiable way of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002630 "reproducing the issue or fix. Patches are always welcome, too."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002631 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002632 "=head2 Where can I go for help with a concrete version?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002633 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002634 "Bugs and feature requests are accepted against the latest version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002635 "only. To get patches for earlier versions, you need to get an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002636 "agreement with a developer of your choice - who may or not report the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002637 "issue and a suggested fix upstream (depends on the license you have"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002638 "chosen)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002639 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002640 "=head2 Business support and maintenance"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002641 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002642 "For business support you can contact Jens via his CPAN email"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002643 "address rehsackATcpan.org. Please keep in mind that business"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002644 "support is neither available for free nor are you eligible to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002645 "receive any support based on the license distributed with this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002646 "package."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002648 "=head1 ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002650 "Jochen Wiedmann created the original module as an XS (C) extension in 1998."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002651 "Jeff Zucker took over the maintenance in 2001 and rewrote all of the C"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002652 "portions in Perl and began extending the SQL support.  More recently Ilya"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002653 "Sterin provided help with SQL::Parser, Tim Bunce provided both general and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002654 "specific support, Dan Wright and Dean Arnold have contributed extensively"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002655 "to the code, and dozens of people from around the world have submitted"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002656 "patches, bug reports, and suggestions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002657 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002658 "In 2008 Jens Rehsack took over the maintenance of the extended module"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002659 "from Jeff.  Together with H.Merijn Brand (who has taken DBD::CSV),"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002660 "Detlef Wartke and Volker Schubbert (especially between 1.16 developer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002661 "versions until 1.22) and all submitters of bug reports via RT a lot of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002662 "issues have been fixed."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002663 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002664 "Thanks to all!"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002665 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002666 "If you're interested in helping develop SQL::Statement or want to use it"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002667 "with your own modules, feel free to contact Jeff or Jens."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002668 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002669 "=head1 BUGS AND LIMITATIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002670 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002671 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002672 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002673 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002674 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002675 "Currently we treat NULL and '' as the same in AnyData/CSV mode -"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002676 "eventually fix."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002678 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002679 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002680 "No nested C-style comments allowed as SQL99 says."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002681 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002682 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002683 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002684 "There are some issues regarding combining outer joins with where"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002685 "clauses."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002686 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002687 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002688 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002689 "Aggregate functions cannot be used in where clause."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002690 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002691 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002692 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002693 "Some SQL commands/features are not supported (most of them cannot by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002694 "design), as C<LOCK TABLE>, using indices, sub-selects etc."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002695 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002696 "Currently the statement for missing features is: I plan to create a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002697 "SQL::Statement v2.00 based on a pure Backus-Naur-Form parser and a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002698 "fully object oriented command pattern based engine implementation."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002699 "When the time is available, I will do it. Until then bugs will be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002700 "fixed or other Perl modules under my maintainership will receive my"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002701 "time. Features which can be added without deep design changes might be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002702 "applied earlier - especially when their addition allows studying"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002703 "effective ways to implement the feature in upcoming 2.00."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002704 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002705 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002706 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002707 "Some people report that SQL::Statement is slower since the XS parts"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002708 "were implemented in pure Perl. This might be true, but on the other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002709 "hand a large number of features have been added including support for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002710 "ANSI SQL 99."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002711 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002712 "For SQL::Statement 1.xx it's not planned to add new XS parts."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002713 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002714 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002715 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002716 "Wildcards are expanded to lower cased identifiers. This might confuse"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002717 "some people, but it was easier to implement."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002718 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002719 "The warning in L<DBI> to never trust the case of returned column names"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002720 "should be read more often. If you need to rely on identifiers, always"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002721 "use C<sth-E<gt>{NAME_lc}> or C<sth-E<gt>{NAME_uc}> - never rely on"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002722 "C<sth-E<gt>{NAME}>:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002723 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002724 "  $dbh->{FetchHashKeyName} = 'NAME_lc';"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002725 "  $sth = $dbh->prepare(\"SELECT FOO, BAR, ID, NAME, BAZ FROM TABLE\");"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002726 "  $sth->execute;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002727 "  $hash_ref = $sth->fetchall_hashref('id');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002728 "  print \"Name for id 42 is $hash_ref->{42}->{name}\\n\";"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002729 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002730 "See L<DBI/FetchHashKeyName> for more information."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002731 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002732 "=item *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002733 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002734 "Unable to use the same table twice with different aliases. B<Workaround>:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002735 "Temporary tables: C<< CREATE TEMP TABLE t_foo AS SELECT * FROM foo >>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002736 "Than both tables can be used independently."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002737 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002738 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002739 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002740 "Patches to fix bugs/limitations (or a grant to do it) would be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002741 "very welcome. Please note, that any patches B<must> successfully pass"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002742 "all the C<SQL::Statement>, L<DBD::File> and L<DBD::CSV> tests and must"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002743 "be a general improvement."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002744 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002745 "=head1 AUTHOR AND COPYRIGHT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002746 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002747 "Jochen Wiedmann created the original module as an XS (C) extension in 1998."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002748 "Jeff Zucker took over the maintenance in 2001 and rewrote all of the C"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002749 "portions in perl and began extending the SQL support. Since 2008, Jens"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002750 "Rehsack is the maintainer."
